# Jak 1: the fingers bending to the world (LIST-0.1.1 items 21 and 35; the owner: "satisfying world collision with
# finger bending to the world"). A new game to Geyser Rock (as jak1_play.sim); the player crouches and looks down, the
# right hand goes to the ground and is turned there: edge on, the palm down (rolled either way), the fingers pointed
# into the ground (pitched down 60 and 85 degrees), then lifted again; last the left hand the same way.
# Run with JAKVR_BODY_TRACE=1: "[vr-body] the right fingers c0..c4, by the world +o0..+o4, at N surfaces" twice a
# second (each finger's curl as drawn and how far the world moved it from what the controller asks, thumb first).
